{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eJH7e6AkjBWVE-zjx",
			"description": "Kabalite Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47): plates riding on a flexible weave, so blunt-trauma rules apply as for Guardian mesh: a hit that fails to penetrate still delivers (damage/10, rounded down, minimum 1) crushing injury.\n\nLore: The light segmented plate of the Kabalite Warrior and most Kabal raiders: overlapping barbed plates over a body glove, giving good protection at very low weight and leaving the wearer free to move and dodge (Codex: Drukhari background). It is much more visible and aggressive than Aeldari mesh but works on the same principle.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor is 'light segmented plate: DR 36, Weak Points 5 (as Guardian mesh)', so torso DR 36 and WP 5 are held exactly, the same mechanical protection as the Aeldari mesh anchor (both are mesh-class protection regardless of who built it). Exact dice: a lasgun hit (7d(2) burn) penetrates the torso 90.6% of the time, a shuriken catapult hit (5d(3) cut) 90.2%, a splinter rifle hit 66.4%, an autogun round (7d pi) only 0.3%, a boltgun 99.8%. Limbs at 29 (lasgun 98.8%, autogun 13.7%), eye lens at 20 as for carapace visors, helmet and neck 30 (as mesh). Hands and feet are small plates at 18 (the Aeldari mesh leaves them unarmoured), an honest reflection of the raider's gauntlets and boots. It is heavier than the Aeldari mesh (9 lb against 6 lb) because it carries plates, not just fibre. An eye hit from a splinter rifle penetrates the lens 98.8% of the time, and counts as a brain hit for piercing damage (B399).",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "900",
