		{
			"id": "eHSqC9XJe065XOy2k",
			"description": "Wychsuit",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47). Covers only the torso and groin; the arms, legs, head and hands are unarmoured. No DX or Stealth penalty. The Wych's protection is her Dodge and Acrobatics, not the suit.\n\nLore: The minimal skintight garb of the Wych Cults: a body suit of thin hide or cloth with a few plates at the vitals, worn because a Wych relies on speed and avoidance rather than on armour (Codex: Drukhari background). It leaves her free to leap, spin and twist through a fight.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor is 'almost no armour: DR 12, flexible', held exactly on the torso, vitals and groin, with everything else left at 0 for freedom of movement. Weak Points 7, the flak rating, since a thin suit has a lot of gaps. Exact dice: DR 12 stops nothing that matters: an autogun round (7d pi) penetrates 99.7%, a splinter rifle hit 99.9%, and a lasgun hit 100.0%; it stops mostly a light blade or a bare-handed blow. Against any real weapon a Wych survives by not being hit. Handling: 2 lb, no ST requirement, no coverage beyond the torso.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Wych Cult"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "300",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
