		{
			"id": "e-OvWn3Uo4YOMKg9z",
			"description": "Ghostplate Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47). Weak personal field, per the framework's Personal force fields rules: 20 SP, recharge after 3 seconds without damage at 5 SP/second, covers all attacks. Field knocked to 0 needs double the delay (6 seconds) before recharging. Track current SP with the Uses counter (max 20). Overflow damage passes to the plate with the attack's full armour divisor.\n\nLore: The armour of Archons and Kabalite Trueborn: lighter than the Kabalite's plate for the protection it gives, and fitted with a weak personal field that dissipates part of an attack's force (Codex: Drukhari background). It is what a Kabal lord who does not trust his warriors wears.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor is 'DR 60, very light, with a weak field': torso DR 60 (between Kabalite plate 36 and Aspect armour 70), limbs 53, helmet 50, eye lens 22 (scaled to the DR as Aspect plate's 25 at DR 70), hands and feet 30. The field is built on the Personal force fields chassis at a fraction of the refractor field's 40 SP: 20 SP, delay 3 seconds, recharge 5 SP/second, covering all attacks. That is deliberately weak: a single lasgun hit (average 24.5) collapses it. Exact dice: torso DR 60 stops a lasgun hit 90.6% of the time, a shuriken hit 77.9%, a splinter rifle hit 97.3%, and a boltgun 9.6% (90.4% penetrate); limbs at 53 are noticeably weaker (lasgun 33.2%, bolter 96.4%). Weak Points 5 as for Kabalite plate: a segmented suit with more seams than Aspect plate (4). Handling: 8 lb, no ST requirement.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal",
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield"
			],
