		{
			"id": "enRGzHRG1WryFw3Vd",
			"description": "Incubus Warsuit",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRigid heavy plate: no blunt-trauma rule. Weak Points 4. Full-body coverage.\n\nLore: The heavy plate of the Incubi: a full suit of thick, ornate armour, much heavier than a Kabalite's and the mark of an elite warrior-cult that expects to fight at the front (Codex: Drukhari background). It is worn with a full helm.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor is 'DR 85, Weak Points 4 (as Exarch armour)', so torso 85 and WP 4 are held exactly and the coverage follows the Exarch profile: limbs 78, helmet and neck 70, eye lens 30, hands and feet 42. Unlike the Exarch suit it is rigid, so the flexible rule is dropped and it weighs 32 lb (an Exarch's 16 lb is a fused wraithbone suit; an Incubus wears plated ceramic and steel). Exact dice: it stops a lasgun hit 100.0% and a shuriken catapult hit 99.9% and a splinter rifle hit 100.0% of the time; a boltgun round penetrates the torso 45.4% and a limb 63.7% of the time (framework: the same as Sororitas plate at 85). Eye lens 30 is at Sororitas parity.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Incubi"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "12000",
			"base_weight": "32 lb",
			"features": [
