		{
			"id": "emDFkLC-a1wAkVIqK",
			"description": "Shadow Field",
			"local_notes": "Regenerating-shield chassis with no regeneration: 200 SP, covers all attacks, does NOT recharge during the fight. Damage from an attack the field covers comes off SP first; if an attack does more damage than the SP remaining, the field drops to 0 and the excess passes to worn armour with the attack's full armour divisor. Once at 0 SP the field is gone for the rest of the fight. Between fights it is restored (an hour of attendants' work, GM's call). Track current SP with the Uses counter (max 200).\n\nLore: An Archon's personal defence: a large shadow-shield that wraps the wearer in darkness and turns aside almost anything, but once broken it does not return in the same fight (Codex: Drukhari background gives it as one-use protection).\n\nDesign: The framework says 'a large shield that does not recharge; when breached it is gone for the fight'. Pool 200 SP, larger than the iron halo's 120 and the storm shield's 160, because it never recovers: over a whole fight an iron halo (120 SP at 20 SP/second) absorbs far more damage, but the Archon's shield takes the first blow. Exact figures: a boltgun hit is 42 average plus a 6d cr ex follow-up of 21 that also comes off SP (framework), so about 3 bolts (63 each) break it; a lasgun hit averages 24.5, so 8 hits; a dark lance hit averages 84, so 2-3. Handling: 2 lb, no ST requirement.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal",
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "30000",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"uses": 200,
			"max_uses": 200,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eJhXW96r_ZmdstYYM",
			"description": "Clone Field",
			"local_notes": "+2 Dodge, applies only against attacks the wearer can see coming (it scatters a visible image, not the wearer's actual position) and not against area or cone effects. Does not stack with a holo-suit or with shield Defense Bonus. Gives no DR.\n\nLore: A personal field that projects false images of the wearer around him, making it hard to tell which is real, worn by Archons and other Drukhari leaders (Codex: Drukhari background gives it as a defensive item). The sources do not say more; this entry follows the framework.\n\nDesign: The framework says 'illusory images: a Dodge bonus, not DR'. Modelled as a flat +2 Dodge (attribute bonus), one below the Aeldari holo-suit's +3, since a clone field is a defensive add-on to real armour rather than the whole basis of the wearer's defence. The visibility and area limitations keep it from being a free upgrade. Handling: 1.5 lb, no ST requirement, no DR.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari"
			],
			"tech_level": "11^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "15000",
			"base_weight": "1.5 lb",
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dodge",
					"amount": 2
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "EqoZrTEDcefriEGLn",
			"description": "Combat Drug Dispenser",
			"local_notes": "Worn on the arm or harness; injects the chosen drug as a free action at the start of a fight. Only one drug per combat: the dispenser does not open a second vial in the same fight. The drugs are the traits Combat Drug: Adrenalight, Combat Drug: Grave Lotus, Combat Drug: Hypex, Combat Drug: Painbringer, Combat Drug: Serpentin and Combat Drug: Splintermind. Their effects are defined there; this item only holds and delivers them. Each has its own Dependency (see the traits), which is what makes regular use a hazard.\n\nLore: A device of the Wych Cults that delivers combat drugs by a needle into the arm, giving the Wych a burst of speed, strength or resistance for the length of a fight (Codex: Drukhari background names the six drugs Adrenalight, Grave Lotus, Hypex, Painbringer, Serpentin and Splintermind). The drugs are habit-forming and are the mark of Wych Cult discipline.\n\nDesign: The framework says: 'Wych Cult dispensers: one drug per combat; each a modest, temporary boost to one attribute or skill set, with a Dependency'. The dispenser is a container (GCS sums the children's weight and cost) holding the six vials as separate 1-use children, so the sheet shows which have been used. The rules of each drug live in the traits, not here, so a trait edit updates all users. Weight 1 lb, cost 3000 for the dispenser and 150 per vial (about 3900 for a full set).",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Wych Cult"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3000",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "e-bDDJnp8FD9I8SeA",
					"description": "Vial: Adrenalight",
					"local_notes": "One dose. Its effect is the trait \"Combat Drug: Adrenalight\" (defined in the Drukhari traits library), which lasts for one combat and carries its own Dependency.\n\nDesign: A single sealed dose, priced as a consumable.",
