		{
			"id": "emx9hZrqeuL3oKBQ5",
			"description": "Soul-Trap",
			"local_notes": "Worn on the harness. The wearer treats each killing within 10 yards of him (by his own hand or a squad-mate's) as a feeding for Soul Thirst purposes, at the GM's discretion, and the death also counts toward advancing Power from Pain in the scene. No effect on the wearer's combat rolls.\n\nLore: A Drukhari device for capturing and holding the soul-essence of the slain so it can be consumed later and the wearer's own soul kept from Slaanesh a little longer (background generally; I recall the name from Drukhari wargear lists but hold the exact mechanism and who carries it with low confidence, so the rules here are a design choice rather than a quotation of any rule).\n\nDesign: The framework's Drukhari overview gives no soul-trap anchor and the sources are thin, so it is written as rules text for the GM to apply rather than a combat statistic, in the way the Aeldari spirit stone is. It ties directly to the Drukhari traits: it feeds Soul Thirst and Power from Pain (the disadvantage and the staged bonus defined in the traits library). Cost 20000 makes it a rare relic. Handling: 1 lb, no ST requirement, no DR.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "20000",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		}
	]
